  "role": "Field battery",
  "summary": "Two standoff racks on an open shoulder truss, with a cannon for direct fire. Lighter than a Cairn and much less forgiving under fire.",
  "lore": "A Trestle wears its repair around the shoulders. Separate launcher bins hang from a bolted crossmember, clear of the old root keel, and a fitter can reach either feed without opening the other. The arrangement came from a quarry walker whose original upper hull could not be recovered. Halloran kept the gun arm for the minutes before a spotter finds a firing lane. The smaller battery follows a moving company more easily than a Cairn, but the foreman paints the same instruction inside every cab: this is not the front rank.",
